# What the agent image build must never see.
#
# The first entries are not about size. A build context is handed to the daemon
# whole before any instruction runs, and the builder stage does `COPY . .`, so
# anything matching these patterns would reach a layer.
#
# An agent generates its identity key on the host and keeps it in its state
# directory. Anybody who has run `CERTPILOT_AGENT_STATE=./state certpilot-agent
# enrol` while working on this repository has an ed25519 private key sitting in
# the tree. A certificate management product baking its own private keys into a
# layer is the specific failure this file prevents — and it is the one failure
# here that deleting the image does not undo, because layers get pushed.
.env
.env.*
.certpilot/
state/
*.pem
*.key

# Not inputs to the binary.
.git/
.github/
bin/
scripts/
*.md
*.log
.DS_Store
